WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.590
Wiping off my tears.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.300
I'm starting to run now

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:18.560
Tomorrow I'll be born anew.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.370
How could "you always be my friend"?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.280
That person's word makes me more courageous.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.480
There are times when it's possible I will be depressed

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.580
and there are times when things are delightful.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:45.170
I'll always be

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.020
next to you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.910
Smiling 100%

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.450
Striking 100%

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.640
I've come so far.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.560
Being 100% pure

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.190
The things I want to tell you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.670
change to treasure completely.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
in the 100% case

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if it's a long distance,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.280
I'll still say I would meet you with the same feelings.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:43.020
Q-Class received a job request from Diet Member Takatobi, who had
received a letter threatening him with the curse of Mayahime.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.100
We arrived at the village soon to be submerged underwater: Jinchuumura.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:51.320
Just as we began the investigation, the client was found dead inside his villa.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:02:00.080
The crime scene was a perfect locked room scenario, with
a giant block of concrete sealing the only entrance.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.080
Is this a legitimate curse?

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:09.960
Our investigation began amidst the complicated relationships
surrounding the construction of the dam.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.170
Village of Traitors

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.140
It’s late.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.100
I’m going to my room.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.180
We'll go too

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.180
Let’s go, Kyuu.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:26.980
Yeah.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.140
'Night.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.060
Good night.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.190
What?

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.570
No way, it was you who killed Takatobi?

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.540
Ouch!

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.420
That really hurt, Meg!

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.300
It wasn’t that bad!

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.050
You hit us with solid wood!

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.010
It’s because you were peeking,

00:02:59.030 --> 00:02:59.800
Jerks.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.100
This is Goura’s room.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.930
Yeah, so what?

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.350
The lights are off.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:12.690
It’s not all that strange, seeing as it’s past 11.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.400
Well, whatever.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.150
Let’s get to sleep.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:18.610
Yeah.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.010
It’s all swelled up...

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.010
Look at what you dd, Meg!

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.970
Whoa, it really swelled up bad.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.520
It’s your fault for doing something stupid.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:52.440
You’re right, I agree!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:52.980
Don’t say that.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.310
Especially you, Kyuu!

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.730
You did the same thing!

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.230
Good morn... Oh my, your face...

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.070
Don’t laugh!

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.700
Yuri-san.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.860
It’s okay!

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:04.450
He brought it upon himself.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.990
I believe it.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.460
Everyone, breakfast is ready.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.880
What happened to your face, Touyama-san?

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:15.630
Well,

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.510
There comes a time when a man cannot speak of personal matters

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.510
Obviously you couldn’t speak about that.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.550
Don’t hit me, Kinta!

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.340
Shut up!

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:26.300
That’s not fair at all!

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.350
What are you doing? You shouldn’t be causing commotion this early.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.270
Sorry. Just...

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.110
It’s coming from over there!

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.240
What’s wrong?

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.000
How awful.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:52.620
What a mess.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.920
Could this a Hitobashira?

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.510
He was burned by the flames of Mayahime?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:11.470
In a town built with so many Hitobashira, this makes sense.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:12.770
Stop it!

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:13.890
No photos!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.440
Aww, come on.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.110
A tragedy caused by the hatred brought about by the dam’s construction

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.320
This is good material for a dramatic article.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.240
You've become truly rotten haven’t you?

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:33.000
I can’t believe you once tried to bring this village back to life with my brother!

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.830
How am I supposed to bring back a village about to be drowned by a lake?

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.460
What did you say?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.210
Hey, cute it out!

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:45.090
DDS will secure this crime scene.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.060
What is the estimated time of death?

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:55.850
Last night, between 11pm and 12am.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:59.810
The cause of death is blood loss, from the lacerations on his wrists.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.450
I see...

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:14.450
Leaving ash in his lungs to make it look like a suicide.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:17.330
It doesn’t “look like” a suicide, it is one.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.460
Do you have any proof?

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.960
If not then please be quiet.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.550
Where’s your teacher anyway?

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.130
He was here until just a second ago—

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.510
More importantly, you were speaking of “proof”.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.140
Whatever, come with me.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.480
The curse of Mayahime compels me;

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:46.490
I shall become a Hitobashira myself along with Takatobi.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.820
This was written before he died?

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:50.950
That’s correct.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:55.790
Obara-san, was there any indication that the
two victims were worried during this time?

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:02.380
Now that you mention it, Takatobi-san was
worried that he may have been cursed.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:09.760
He was actually a fragile person, he asked Goura-san to
be very thorough and have a priest ward off spirits.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.180
Wait, Detective Mine.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:12.890
What?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.100
Do you have anything else to say?

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:19.560
Do you really believe something as deliberate as this is authentic?

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:24.770
Considering the state of the bodies too, I don’t
think that that’s natural behavior for a suicide.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:27.360
What of it?

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.990
People who commit suicide are already acting unnaturally.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.660
So you think it’s strange too?

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.700
Then what is your evidence to support it being a suicide?

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:41.620
It’s impossible.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:48.050
The police investigated the sealed room crime scene thoroughly too.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:52.840
You also determined that it was impossible to
demonstrate any type of murder took place.

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:57.520
You're saying that because murder must be impossible no matter
how strange their deaths were, suicide is your only conclusion?

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.770
Exactly.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.850
There was a body in a locked room with no way out.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.310
Murder is impossible.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:06.070
So we think it’s a suicide.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.440
That’s what the police think, indeed.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.030
Ah, so you understand, Sensei.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:15.200
But isn’t suicide impossible too?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:20.000
He shouldn’t have been able to move that huge block of concrete himself.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.290
It’s not impossible.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.290
)We'll show that ourselves later.

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:26.920
If you doubt me, feel free to watch.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:35.930
The reason we can’t solve the mystery is because
we're missing something important.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.470
I leave it in your hands.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.100
What do you mean?

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:51.690
Hey, what do we do?

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:55.660
At this rate that arrogant detective is going to write this off as a suicide.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.830
Even though this situation mikes no sense.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:03.790
Just like Hongou-sensei says, I really feel
like we're forgetting something essential.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.710
There’s something that’s been bothering me
this whole time but I can’t figure it out!

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.880
Then let’s clarify that!

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.420
I'll help you, Kyuu.

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:13.970
You can ask me anything!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.140
I remember everything that I’ve seen clearly since we've arrived here.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.140
Meg—

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:21.560
All right, I'll check things out too.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:27.110
The victim may have left dying message that has yet to be found.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:30.070
Then I'll work with Kazuma.

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:33.530
OK, then leave questioning people about the motive to me.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:37.280
While we can’t do this alone, together the five of us can solve it!

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:40.580
If we all work together I’m sure we can do It

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.750
That’s right.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.500
We can still do this without Hongou-sensei!

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:47.670
<i>Companions. . .</i>

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:49.630
Alright!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.130
Now I’m motivated!

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:54.760
Get our DDS badges and move out!

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:01.600
DDS, Q-Class! Let’s go!

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:07.310
Leaving a message before your death huh.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:10.940
Goura-san may have been attacked here.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:16.570
So I was thinking he may have tried to leave
a message before he lost consciousness

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:19.780
But wouldn’t the police have checked that?

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:23.200
If it’s here, it may be hidden as some kind of code.

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:25.250
It wouldn’t be surprising if they missed it.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:31.170
This is the fax he received before he was killed?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:34.340
Huh?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.880
The pages are all out of order.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.130
Why could that be?

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.550
These back markings...

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.180
Could it be?

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.690
I knew it!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.020
What's wrong?

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:56.110
Look at the markings on the paper’s edge.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.530
That’s not from the fax.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:03.410
Yeah, I think Goura-san may have written something here.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:11.790
In other words, the victim wrote something on the
edge without attracting the murderer’s attention.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:14.960
He then scattered them to stop the murderer from noticing the writing.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.930
Let’s line up the fax pages in order!

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.060
It’s done.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:26.720
Lemme see.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.690
What’s this?

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.440
“Kashiya”?

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:38.840
This doesn't help!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:39.960
Look at this Ryuu-kun!

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.910
This fax is from Kashiya Design’s office.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.410
He probably only wrote this to Organize his papers.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:50.080
But why is only the “Ya” written in hiragana?

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.750
Just a mistake?

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.750
Then where do we begin, Kyuu?

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.050
Let’s start with last night when Goura-san was killed.

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:03.850
Now that I think about it, we walked in front of his room.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.010
What time was that?

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:05.850
Wait a moment.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.310
10:45.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:16.270
Meg, did you take a look at the fax that came for him?

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:17.650
Yes, of course.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.650
Then do you know what time it arrived?

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.150
Let me think.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.080
It said 10:30.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.450
I see,

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:34.750
If they sent it that late, it must be a pretty important document night?

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:36.040
I think so too.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.510
He would’ve probably been looking through it that night.

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:40.420
Right?

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:44.470
But when we passed by there, the lights were off.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:51.020
Hey, the criminal may have been there during that time.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.350
I see.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:52.980
That’s right!

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:56.060
Then we can explain it!

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:59.530
The incredibly unnatural actions that a certain person took.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.200
Then you know who the criminal is?

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:06.070
But the motive isn’t certain yet.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:25.760
What are you doing?

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:26.510
Touyama-san!

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.050
You’re Musashi!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.810
Let me go!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.980
Swinging sticks around like that is dangerous!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:35.730
Shut up!

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.190
What did you say, stupid kid?

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.150
Stop it!

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.110
Yuri-san, he tried to hit you.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:45.400
I’m the one at fault.

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.450
Ask her why!

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.370
Y r-san, what’s®going on here?

00:13:57.230 --> 00:14:02.960
Musashi-kun’s older brother was leading demonstrators
against a dam being constructed downstream.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:07.010
During this time, he was suddenly caught in an avalanche and was killed.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:12.930
That dam was also a project forced through by
Kagaki Construction and Diet Member Takatobi.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:24.030
Musashi-kun’s brother Yamato-san, along with Jinnai-san, tried their
best to protect this village and the natural state of the river.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.650
Wait!

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:30.620
Yuri-san, aren’t you Takatobi’s secretary and in favor of—

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.290
No!

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:34.830
Yamato-san and I were lovers!

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:39.460
And this was the town I was born in!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:43.710
I became his secretary to try and stop the construction of the dam!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:50.510
Takatobi didn’t budge when Yaniamoto and Jjinnai started their movement.

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:54.100
I thought I'd try another way,

00:14:55.540 --> 00:15:03.070
but even as his secretary when I tried to question
the need for a dam.. He laughed and said this

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:07.110
“The dam, you see, is necessary.”

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:14.660
“Not for the locals, but for the construction companies
that support me along with myself.”

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:17.370
What a jerk!

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:19.750
I’m an idea.

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:28.470
In the end, not only was I unable to stop him from constructing the
dam, but ironically I ended up helping create it as his secretary.

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:30.300
Yuri-san...

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:37.140
All I can do now for him is visit this small grave.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:41.560
I hated those two, Takatobi and Goura.

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.860
No, not only me.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.780
Everyone hated them.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.070
Musashi-kun, who lost his brother.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.160
Jinnai-san, who lost his friend.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:58.660
Natsumi-san, who lost her father to an accident
at the same place Yamato-san lost his life.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:05.880
I’m sure of it, they all hated Takatobi and Goura enough to kill them.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:12.930
The flames of hatred from all the people who
were made miserable for a useless dam.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:18.810
Yes, the flames of a Hitobashira that burn more violently than Mayahime.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.310
That was what burned them.

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:37.280
Every one of them had a motive.

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:40.580
And the person who took the unnatural actions—

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.080
Cheer up!

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:49.260
Just one more step. If only we had definitive
proof we could identify the criminal!

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:56.100
It’s time for Detective Mine to show us his idea of how the suicide occurred.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:02.350
At this rate, we'll end up losing to the criminal’s trick!

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:08.730
But to catch them we need to solve the mystery of that locked room.

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:14.490
The police have given up on solving the
mystery, can the five of us do it alone?

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:22.660
The police may give up if it’s impossible, but we're detectives.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.920
If a detective gives up, the case will never be solved!

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:38.600
Then I'll begin.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.260
Look closely.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.850
You three move it.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:46.150
Three people? Takatobi was alone

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:47.480
Shut up and watch.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:51.360
After he resigned himself to suicide,

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.530
he hired three people to move this concrete block for him,

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:57.490
paying them a large amount of money to silence them.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.870
This is heavy!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:07.630
Why would he have to do that in order to kill himself?

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:09.840
In order to eliminate the possibility that his death would be seen as murder.

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:15.090
That way the people in the village who opposed the
construction of the dam wouldn’t be suspected.

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:19.220
Did he look like such a nice guy, that politician?

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.060
I don’t think judging by his looks is a good idea...

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.100
What's wrong?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:26.640
Even with three people you can’t move it?

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.480
No, it’s just a little difficult to move in here.

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.940
One, two...

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:34.360
Wait, Detective Mine.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:39.450
Even if they did carry it there, the block would
now be blocking the door from closing.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:42.030
We know.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.450
So they put it in the room.

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:48.460
They then closed the door and he moved it.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:50.250
He moved it alone?

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.710
Of course he did it alone.

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:55.260
And there you go.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.800
He couldn’t move it by himself, could he?

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:59.890
That’s a huge concrete block.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:04.600
You, the big stupid one.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.310
Are you familiar with how the pyramids were constructed?

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:13.900
The pyramids, are made of giant blocks piled on top of each other.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.490
The same way they moved those huge blocks.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.410
Oh I get it!

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:22.740
They used rollers.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.370
Yes. Just like the elementary school kid says.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:31.460
It would be easy to move the concrete block if it were placed on rollers.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:36.630
Well, getting it on the dirt floor would be a
little difficult, but he could’ve managed it.

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:37.630
OK, Try it.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.010
Watch out!

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.520
The floor broke!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:51.310
Impossible.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.940
Was it weakened by the fire?

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.900
Nope.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:01.910
This floor’s just made out of scrap wood.

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:06.740
A heavy block like this would not be supported by this floor.

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:11.830
It looks like suicide has become impossible then, Detective Mine.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.670
I can’t believe it.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.960
Suicide and murder are both impossible.

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:23.220
It can’t be. A perfect locked room.

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:28.140
The mystery’s become even more complicated!

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.230
No way,

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:33.350
could this truly be a curse?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:42.320
The cursed flames of Mayahime, the Hitobashira herself
who protected the village, is what killed them.

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:45.780
Kyuu!

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.450
Ryuu, look at this!

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.250
A vinyl sheet is stuck on the bottom of the concrete block.

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:58.090
You’re right.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:01.760
There’s burnt vinyl on the dirt floor too

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.890
This is a great hint!

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:07.180
It’s all falling together now.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:08.600
There’s no doubt!

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:12.140
This locked room isn’t the curse of Mayahime.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:13.640
It’s a trick!

00:21:22.430 --> 00:21:23.360
We're back.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:27.370
A fax is here for Amakusa-sama..

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.870
It’s the autopsy results I asked for.

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:33.040
Everyone, you can go back to your rooms!

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:34.750
Hey, let me come too!

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:39.960
It’s still on page 5.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.630
There’s quite a bit.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:45.130
That’s page 6.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:47.390
Wait a minute,

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:50.390
the later pages come out on top!

00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:53.980
Then this fax is in reverse, which means

00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:56.020
That’s right!

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.650
That scribble was,

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:59.480
a dying message!

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:02.690
You've solved the mystery of that locked room?

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:04.650
Really, Kyuu?

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:06.200
Yes, I did.

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:11.450
And we've got solid proof of who the criminal is.

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:14.370
Just like I thought, it was there!

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:15.830
Look.

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:18.880
This is the dying message that Goura-san left.

00:22:21.530 --> 00:22:22.710
Amazing!

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:24.260
This is conclusive!

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:25.520
Kyuu!

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:28.430
Let’s get ready and get everyone together.

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:30.600
We're going to face the real criminal!

00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:37.390
Uh, DDS members, what exactly are you going to do?

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:41.400
I need to get ready for the diet member’s funeral.

00:22:41.420 --> 00:22:45.360
I’m going to miss my train too...

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:48.610
Have you found the criminal?

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:50.820
That sounds fun. Quite a scoop.

00:22:53.270 --> 00:22:56.500
Didn’t Takatobi-sense: and Goura-san commit suicide?

00:22:56.520 --> 00:23:00.460
No, their deaths are clearly murders.

00:23:01.150 --> 00:23:02.500
Hey, kid.

00:23:02.530 --> 00:23:06.470
Who gave you permission to put on this little play?

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:08.630
We've found it!

00:23:08.660 --> 00:23:11.600
The criminal’s identity, and proof to support it.

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:16.140
And the answer to the trick that made that
perfect locked room murder possible!

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:18.100
What?

00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:19.980
There are 3 hints.

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:24.320
The first is the unnatural actions that a certain person took.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:27.530
The second is the order the faxes arrive.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:32.760
The third is vinyl sheet under the concrete block.

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:41.750
There is only one answer!

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.770
Somehow it's collapsing

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.140
Embracing such a feeling.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.030
Flowing.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:58.910
I'd be worried tomorrow.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.120
If the same thing happened.

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.120
Go wrong.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:06.460
He looks up at the sky, pondering

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.020
You're very far away.

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:13.180
Show your heart if you have the courage

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.310
passing the border line.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:19.760
In order to get past, I walk against the wind

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.400
and I can finish a battle.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:26.940
When I feel like an abandoned child

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:30.360
then I'll stand in line with you.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.930
Facing the wind, I forget,

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:37.540
somehow this is the only important thing.

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:40.290
We protect, because there Is no return.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.890
It's becoming dearly.

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:45.840
Today I embrace, right now I conquer.

00:24:47.710 --> 00:24:50.940
The brilliant trick used in the perfect locked room is revealed.

00:24:49.920 --> 00:24:56.030
Next Episode

00:24:50.970 --> 00:24:53.950
And the surprising true identity of the real criminal.

00:24:53.970 --> 00:24:57.410
And the daunting pot that lurks at the base of the dam construction.

00:24:57.430 --> 00:25:00.580
The final Hitobashira offer themselves to the cursed flames.

00:25:01.310 --> 00:25:03.870
And there Pluto reveals itself again!

00:25:04.730 --> 00:25:06.290
There’s only one answer!

00:25:06.980 --> 00:25:08.300
That’s impossible!

00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:09.710
I can’t believe it!

00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:12.720
Impossible! It just can’t be!

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:16.890
Yuri-san had a boyfriend!

00:25:16.910 --> 00:25:19.680
Kinta, you really do like older women.

00:25:20.330 --> 00:25:20.970
So do you.
